<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Checking in on Health</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Using Health Technology to Form Good Habits</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Outline strategies for personal development. Interactive: Create a study guide, collaboratively, on various topics.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can outline strategies for personal development related to health and balance in a well-organized text (e.g., "To maintain a healthy lifestyle, I plan to exercise three times a week using a tracker, eat balanced meals, and practice mindfulness daily.")
Can collaboratively create a study guide on health and wellness topics, incorporating tips and strategies (e.g., "Include sections on stress management techniques, like deep breathing exercises and time management tips.")
Can write reflections on personal habits and suggest improvements by using health technology to achieve better life balance (e.g., "I have been staying up too late, so I use a sleep tracker to set a better bedtime routine.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 30%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 20%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays various images of health technology (e.g., smartwatches, meditation apps, hydration trackers, sleep monitors). Students, in pairs, write down 2-3 potential benefits and 1-2 drawbacks of using such technology to improve their "well-being" or "fitness" and briefly share their ideas with their partner.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to write a simple sentence using the Present Perfect Continuous and a modal for possibility related to health tech. For example, the teacher writes: "I <b>have been using</b> a sleep <b>tracker</b> for a month, and I've noticed my <b>sleep patterns</b>. If I had more data, I <b>could improve</b> my restorative <b>sleep</b>." The teacher explicitly highlights the voiced /b/ sound in "benefit" and the voiceless /p/ sound in "pattern" and "practice" when saying the sentences aloud, focusing on sentence rhythm for the present perfect continuous.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What kind of verb tense is 'have been using' and what does it tell us?" (It's the Present Perfect Continuous, and it tells us about an ongoing action or habit that started in the past and continues to the present.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When do we use words like 'could' or 'might' when giving suggestions about health?" (We use them to suggest possibilities or recommendations politely, not strong obligations, considering others' beliefs.)</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Checking in on Health"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short blog post (approx. 200 words) from a popular health and wellness app, titled "Boosting Your Balance with Tech: A Teen's Guide to Better Habits." The article discusses how various apps and trackers can help improve aspects like "hydration," "mindfulness," "activity level," and "diet," providing examples of suggestions and hypothetical situations. It implicitly uses Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, and modals for possibility.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Comprehend and analyze written information related to health technology and personal development strategies.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (written):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist:</b> Students read the blog post and write a one-sentence summary explaining its main idea.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read several statements about the text and write "True" or "False." (e.g., "The article suggests that all health apps are reliable." "The text mentions tracking food intake as a way to improve diet.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Students match specific health technologies mentioned in the text (e.g., "sleep tracker," "hydration app") with the health habit they help improve (e.g., "consistent sleep pattern," "regular water intake"). They write down the matched pairs.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Writing sentences and short paragraphs using Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, and Modals for possibility. Vocabulary: <i>tracker, app, habit, routine, balance, mindfulness, hydration, fitness, well-being, stress, exercise, sleep, practice, maintain, improve, track, support, boost, recommend, could, might, should</i>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice: Sentence Completion & Transformation.</b> Students receive a worksheet with incomplete sentences or sentences requiring transformation. They complete sentences with the correct form of the verb (Present Perfect Continuous) or choose the appropriate modal/conditional to form logical, grammatically correct sentences related to health technology and habits.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 1: "I ______ (exercise) regularly to boost my <b>energy</b> levels since I started using my <b>fitness tracker</b>." (<i>I <b>have been exercising</b> regularly to boost my <b>energy</b> levels...</i>)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 2: "If I ______ (monitor) my <b>diet</b> more closely, I ______ (feel) more <b>energized</b>." (<i>If I <b>monitored</b> my <b>diet</b> more closely, I <b>would feel</b> more <b>energized</b>.</i>)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 3: "You ______ (try) a <b>meditation app</b> to <b>manage stress</b>; it ______ (support) your <b>well-being</b>." (<i>You <b>could/might try</b> a <b>meditation app</b> to <b>manage stress</b>; it <b>might support</b> your <b>well-being</b>.</i>)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice: Expanding on Health Habits.</b> The teacher provides sentence starters or key phrases related to using health technology. Students individually write 2-3 complete sentences, expanding on the ideas while incorporating the target grammar (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, modals) and vocabulary.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Starter 1: "Since I started using a sleep <b>tracker</b>..." (e.g., "Since I started using a sleep <b>tracker</b>, I <b>have been analyzing</b> my <b>sleep patterns</b>. If I adjusted my <b>bedtime routine</b>, I <b>might achieve</b> a more <b>restorative sleep</b>.")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Starter 2: "To <b>improve</b> my <b>hydration</b>, I..." (e.g., "To <b>improve</b> my <b>hydration</b>, I <b>have been setting</b> daily <b>reminders</b> on my <b>app</b>. I <b>should also consider</b> carrying a water bottle with me to <b>maintain</b> <b>consistent</b> intake.")</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Collaborative Peer Check & Edit.</b> Students work in pairs. Each student writes a short paragraph (4-5 sentences) reflecting on one personal health habit they "have been trying to improve" using technology, and "what they would do if they had more time/resources" for their "well-being" or "fitness." They then exchange paragraphs, carefully reading and providing written feedback to their partner. Feedback should check for correct use of Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, modals for possibility, and target vocabulary, as well as clarity and organization. Students practice giving polite suggestions (e.g., "You <b>might want</b> to check the tense here," "<b>Could</b> you explain how this <b>app supports</b> your <b>fitness</b>?").</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Checking in on Health"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Collaborative creation of a "Personalized Health Technology Study Guide."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b> Students work in groups of 3-4. Their task is to collaboratively write a study guide (250-300 words) for their peers titled "Tech-Enhanced Well-being: Your Guide to Healthier Habits." The guide must outline strategies for personal development related to health and balance, incorporating tips and suggestions. It connects directly to the theme "Using Health Technology to Form Good Habits" and the scenario "Checking in on Health."</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The guide should include sections on at least three different areas (e.g., "Hydration Habits," "Mindful Movement," "Restorative Sleep," "Stress Management").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each section must:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Explain how technology <b>has been used</b> to track or improve that specific habit (using Present Perfect Continuous, e.g., "We <b>have been tracking</b> our <b>activity levels</b> with smartwatches...").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Suggest <b>hypothetical improvements</b> or benefits if the technology or routine were followed more consistently (using Second Conditional, e.g., "If students consistently used a <b>hydration app</b>, they <b>would maintain</b> better daily <b>hydration</b>.").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Offer <b>specific recommendations</b> using modals of possibility (e.g., <b>might, could, should</b>) for how peers can implement these habits, using formal and polite language (e.g., "You <b>might want</b> to download a <b>mindfulness app</b>..."). Students should also use polite expressions like, "It sounds tough, but you <b>could try</b> this..." to express empathy and understanding.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students must integrate at least 10 words from the target vocabulary list (e.g., <i>tracker, app, well-being, mindfulness, balance, routine, maintain, improve, recommend, self-care, consistent, energize</i>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Emphasis is placed on writing a well-organized, coherent text with clear topic sentences and supporting details, demonstrating their ability to outline strategies effectively.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher observation during collaborative writing and a rubric for evaluating the submitted "Personalized Health Technology Study Guide."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their group's collaboratively written "Personalized Health Technology Study Guide."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and Organization:</b> Is the guide well-structured, logically organized, and easy for peers to understand? (Addressing "Can outline strategies for personal development related to health and balance in a well-organized text.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Content & Cohesion:</b> Does it effectively outline strategies for personal development related to health and balance, incorporating diverse tips and suggestions? (Addressing "Can collaboratively create a study guide on health and wellness topics, incorporating tips and strategies.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar Accuracy:</b> Accurate and appropriate use of Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, and Modals for possibility.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary Use:</b> Appropriate and varied use of target vocabulary (e.g., <i>hydration, mindfulness, balance, tracker, recommend, improve, consistent, preventive</i>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pragmatic & Sociolinguistic:</b> Effective use of polite suggestions, empathetic language, and formal expressions when discussing health.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration:</b> Evidence of active group participation and shared contribution to the written product.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket (written):</b> Students individually answer the following prompts:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "What was one new strategy for personal health development that I outlined in our guide, and how might I apply it in my own life?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "Reflect on your contribution to the study guide. How effectively did you use the target grammar (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, modals) and vocabulary in your writing?"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt (written):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "What was the most challenging part of writing the health technology study guide, and how did our group overcome it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "How has this lesson changed your perspective on using technology to monitor and improve your personal <b>health</b> and <b>well-being</b>, particularly regarding setting <b>consistent habits</b> and finding <b>balance</b>?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> "The students generally demonstrated good comprehension of the input text and were able to identify key strategies. The practice activities successfully guided them toward using the target grammar structures (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, modals) in written form, especially when discussing ongoing habits and hypothetical improvements. Some groups still need more explicit instruction on paragraph structuring and using cohesive devices to create a truly 'well-organized text' at the B1.3 level. Peer feedback was helpful, but I need to reinforce the specific criteria for constructive written criticism further. The main production task yielded varied results; some groups excelled in outlining strategies clearly and integrating a wide range of vocabulary, while others focused more on descriptive rather than prescriptive language. I will need to ensure more structured peer review before the final draft in future writing lessons."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> "This lesson's focus on outlining strategies and collaborative writing for a study guide will directly prepare students for the mediation and integration tasks in Lesson 5. They will adapt their written guides into a presentation or a summary report for a wider audience, consolidating information and applying their 21st-century skills."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>